🌏 AI Hybrid Travel Assistant – Vietnam Tourism (RAG-Powered)

An intelligent hybrid RAG-based Travel Assistant that combines vector search, graph databases, and LLMs to provide rich, context-aware travel recommendations for Vietnam.
This project demonstrates how AI can enhance tourism insights using Pinecone, Neo4j, and GPT-4o-mini.

🧩 Overview

This assistant analyzes Vietnam’s tourism knowledge base using:

Semantic vector search (Pinecone)

Graph-based relationship awareness (Neo4j)

LLM reasoning (GPT-4o-mini)

The system answers complex queries such as:
“Best beaches for family trips near Da Nang?”
“Top-rated activities around Hoi An with hotels nearby?”

It uses more than 350+ travel entities across major destinations in Vietnam.

⚙️ Features
🔍 Hybrid Retrieval System

Pinecone vector search for semantic matching

Neo4j graph traversal for relationship enrichment

GPT-4o-mini for natural language answers

🗺️ Rich Dataset Coverage

350+ travel entities

Cities: Hanoi, Ha Long Bay, Hoi An, Da Nang, Nha Trang, Ho Chi Minh City

Metadata: descriptions, tags, visit times, attractions, hotels

10+ relationship types (Located_In, Connected_To, Available_In, etc.)

🧠 Intelligent Query Processing

Semantic ranking of travel entities

Graph neighborhood expansion for deeper context

RAG-style merged context fed into GPT-4o-mini

Citation-backed responses for traceability

🖥️ Developer Tools

Interactive CLI

Graph visualization (HTML)

Batch vector uploads

Entity-level metadata management

🏗️ Architecture
Core Components

Vector Database (Pinecone)

Stores 1536-dimensional semantic embeddings

Fast cosine similarity search

Serverless (AWS us-east-1)

Graph Database (Neo4j)

Entities + relationships modeling

Multi-hop traversal for context

Nodes enriched with metadata

Language Model (OpenAI GPT-4o-mini)

Answers in natural language

Low-temperature factual mode

Citation-friendly responses

🔄 Workflow
Phase 1 – Setup

API setup for Neo4j, Pinecone, OpenAI

Prepared vietnam_travel_dataset.json

Installed required Python libraries

Phase 2 – Data Ingestion

Vector Upload

Generated embeddings (text-embedding-3-small)

Created serverless Pinecone index

Uploaded vectors in batches of 32

Graph Loading

Created Neo4j nodes with dual labels

Set uniqueness constraints

Created directional relationships

Graph Visualization

HTML-based relationship graph

Phase 3 – Query Pipeline

User enters travel question

Query converted to embedding

Pinecone retrieves top 5 semantic matches

Neo4j fetches related entities

Combined context fed to LLM

GPT-4o-mini generates a final answer with citations

